From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:14:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] images: do not bind the host's EGL over a MAINLINE vendor

mount_rootfs() bind-mounts the host's /vendor/lib*/egl over the
container's on every host that has one. That is meant for vendor images
that run on host vendor blobs. A MAINLINE vendor image ships its own
EGL, and the bind hides it.

On the BraX3, a Halium host whose vendor type comes out MAINLINE, the
container saw only the host's Mali libraries. They are of no use with
the image's gralloc. SurfaceFlinger and hwcomposer aborted with
"couldn't find an OpenGL ES implementation", and Android never booted.

Skip the bind when the vendor type is MAINLINE.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 tools/helpers/images.py | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tools/helpers/images.py b/tools/helpers/images.py
index 807cdde..21712cb 100644
--- a/tools/helpers/images.py
+++ b/tools/helpers/images.py
@@ -235,7 +235,14 @@ def mount_rootfs(args, images_dir, session):
                                     upper_dir=tools.config.defaults["overlay_rw"] + "/vendor",
                                     work_dir=tools.config.defaults["overlay_work"] + "/vendor")
 
+    # The host's EGL is only of use with a vendor image built against host
+    # vendor blobs. A MAINLINE vendor brings its own (Mesa, ANGLE), and the
+    # bind hides them: on a Halium host whose vendor type comes out MAINLINE
+    # the container saw only the host's Mali libraries, could not load the
+    # renderer its props name, and SurfaceFlinger aborted.
     for egl_path in ["/vendor/lib/egl", "/vendor/lib64/egl"]:
+        if cfg["waydroid"]["vendor_type"] == "MAINLINE":
+            break
         if os.path.isdir(egl_path):
             helpers.mount.bind(
                 args, egl_path, tools.config.defaults["rootfs"] + egl_path)
